# EPIC: Autonomous Optical FRQ Capture, Deterministic Verification & Progressive AI Grading Pipeline

**Objective:** Deliver a zero-friction, end-to-end handwritten Free Response Question (FRQ) ingestion and grading system for AP STEM examinations (AP Calculus AB/BC, Physics, Chemistry) that achieves >99% rubric-level accuracy through deterministic computer vision, Computer Algebra System (CAS) verification, and a three-stage rollout from human-in-the-loop MVP to autonomous AI grading.

---

## 1. Architectural Foundation (Implemented — Stage 1 Ready)

The end-to-end physical-to-digital capture, rectification, and human-in-the-loop grading infrastructure is implemented and operational in production:

### A. Optical Capture & Perspective Rectification

* **Zero-Tap Mobile Scanner (`components/scanner/MobileCameraView.tsx`):** Performs real-time Laplacian blur filtering, specular glare checks, 4-corner fiducial geometry locking, `1.2s` (`6 × 200ms`) steady-frame verification, `50ms` 3-frame sharpest-burst capture, and fiducial-guided 4-digit Code-128C (`QQPP`) barcode decoding. Verified sheets upload directly to S3 via pre-signed POST URLs with zero manual confirmation taps.


* **Fiducial Registration & Homography Warping (`lib/cv/fiducials.ts`, `lib/frq/cropper.ts`):** Detects the four `8mm × 8mm` corner registration targets using white-paper quiet-zone halos, internal quadrilateral invariants, and the Top-Left L-cutout orientation signature. Warps captured photos onto a canonical `1700 × 2200` (200 DPI US Letter) canvas and extracts individual sub-part crops (`Slot 1` / `Slot 2`).


* **Session Lifecycle & End-of-Exam Hand-Off (`actions/frqCapture.ts`, `components/exam/SectionCaptureModal.tsx`):** Enforces a 45-minute `ACTIVE` capture session window per test attempt, locks sessions to `CAPTURED` upon finalization to prevent post-submission overwrites, and aggregates `FrqSubCrop` scores into `Response`, `Result`, and `TestSummary` records.



### B. Deterministic Verification & Atomic Rubric Schema

* **Atomic Rubric Schema (`types/content.ts`, `content/ap_calc/.../*.md`):** Structures each FRQ sub-part in section Markdown frontmatter into binary, single-point scoring criteria (`id`, `description`, `points`, `expectedLatex`, `numericTolerance`, `requiredUnits`, `requiresJustification`, `allowConsequentialCarryover`).


* **Gate 1 — Deterministic Blank-Box Detector (`lib/frq/inkCheck.ts`):** Evaluates interior dark ink pixel density (`luminance < 165`, inset `16px` to ignore border lines and faint `RGB(235,235,235)` dot grids). Crops with `< 0.35%` ink ratio automatically score `0 / pointsPossible` (`transcription: "[Blank]"`, `needsHumanAudit: false`) with zero human or LLM intervention.
* **Gate 3 — Pure-TypeScript Symbolic & Numeric CAS Verifier (`lib/frq/casVerifier.ts`):** Uses `nerdamer` to normalize student LaTeX expressions and deterministically verify algebraic equivalence (`simplify((a) - (b)) === 0`), AP 3-decimal numeric rounding tolerance (`±0.001`), univariate function probing, and step-to-step arithmetic consistency.

### C. Stage 1: Human-in-the-Loop MVP (`lib/frq/evaluator.ts`, `app/tgadmin/frq-audit/`)

* **Controlled Rollout Flag (`ACTIVE_GRADING_STAGE = "STAGE_1_HUMAN_MVP"`):** Routes every non-blank sub-part crop to `/tgadmin/frq-audit` (`needsHumanAudit: true`, `auditReason: "STAGE_1_HUMAN_GRADING"`) pre-populated with its exact `.md` atomic rubric checklist.


* **One-Click Tutor Audit Workspace (`AuditQueueClient.tsx`, `actions/frqAudit.ts`):** Displays the cropped handwriting alongside the rectified full-sheet toggle, collapsible question prompt, target answer keys, and clickable rubric criterion checkboxes. Tutors award points with single clicks (zero manual LaTeX entry required), generating a structured gold-standard dataset of `(cropImage, humanRubricBreakdown, pointsAwarded)` for Stage 2 benchmarking.



